WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 5: Tell Me How.

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.540
Welcome to Unit 5!

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:11.000
In this unit, you will explore the world
of instructional and procedural writing.

4
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.380
Procedural texts are everywhere around us.

5
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:21.200
They tell us how to cook a meal, how to play a game, how to
build something, and how to get from one place to another.

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:28.400
Every time you follow a recipe, read a science
experiment, or look at the instructions for a board game,

7
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.600
you are reading a procedural text.

8
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:39.060
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read, understand,
and write your own clear and well-organised instructions.

9
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.280
You will also learn an important grammar
pattern called the zero conditional,

10
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.680
which is used to describe things that are always true.

11
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:54.160
This unit will strengthen your reading, writing,
speaking, and listening skills, all through the lens...

12
00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:00.560
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:07.540
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read
and understand procedural and instructional texts,

14
00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.440
identifying their key features and structure.

15
00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:18.060
you will also recognise and use imperative
verbs (command words) such as cut, stir, place,

16
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.840
and measure in your own writing.

17
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:28.280
you will also identify and use time connectives (first,
next, then, after that, finally) to sequence steps clearly.

18
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.060
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:39.740
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: communicate,
quote, emphasize, persuade, convince, encourage.

20
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.420
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

21
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.040
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

22
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:57.320
The reading sequence includes Tell Me How:
source text 1 and Tell Me How: source text 2.

23
00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.740
Read actively.

24
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.840
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

25
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.960
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

26
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.400
The first language focus is What is the Zero Conditional?.

27
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:19.360
The zero conditional is a type of conditional sentence
that we use to talk about things that are always true.

28
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:27.400
These include scientific facts, rules of nature, and general
truths that happen every time a certain condition is met.

29
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:34.060
We call it the “zero” conditional because there
is zero chance that the result will not happen.

30
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.500
If the condition is true, the result is always true.

31
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:45.520
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

32
00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.940
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: The Instruction Game (Pairs).

33
00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:57.960
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

34
00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.800
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

35
00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.600
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

36
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.080
You are ready to begin.

37
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.600
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

38
00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.560
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

39
00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.880
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
